  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "label": "Shade-aware versus original all-cutoff color matching",
  "description": "Paired comparisons of original Euclidean OKLab measurements and newly indexed shade-aware measurements. Four bucket counts, blend exponents 0/3/6, and power quality influence 1/3, plus the new registered default. Both methods globally rank the complete 545-asset corpus in real OpenSearch using the same all-cutoff formula. Existing single-observer development judgments only; no inferred preferences for the two newly reported dark-red examples. Small-corpus latency does not establish million-record scalability.",
